= Appendix A: Full quantitative analysis

*Method.* The real-CTD model (`analysis/basis_trade_real_ctd.py`) prices the CTD on its real coupon calendar (Feb 15 / Aug 15), settlement 11 Nov 2026, first coupon 15 Feb 2027 (96 of 184 days into the half-year): dirty price = Σ CF/(1+y/2)^(w+k); clean = dirty − accrued; DV01 and duration by ±1 bp repricing. Basis G = P(cash) − CF × F(futures). Hedge: short futures DV01-matched, n = DV01_cash / DV01_futures = 887 contracts (equivalently 1,000 × CF), each \$100,000 face. One contract's DV01 is the CTD's DV01 divided by CF (≈\$62.04/bp); the 887 contracts' DV01 totals \$55,034/bp, exactly the cash leg's DV01. The 887 contracts deliver \$88.7m face at expiry; the remaining \$11.3m face is sold for cash at delivery, after the basis has converged, so it carries no residual basis risk. Repo borrowing = dirty market value × (1 − h); equity = dirty market value × h; leverage = 1/h. Base-case P&L is computed leg by leg by exact repricing at delivery (same yield, G = 0): cash P&L +\$250,268, futures P&L +\$15,755, repo cost −\$198,173, total +\$67,850. The script asserts this equals carry + basis P&L (gap −\$1,731, the unhedged-residual rounding). The par illustration (`analysis/basis_trade.py`, corrected 2026-11-11) uses the same formulas on a 10-year par bond; its base case is −\$80,000 after the basis-sign correction.

*Inputs and data vintage.* CTD: 3 7/8% 8/15/2033, CUSIP 91282CHT1, coupon 3.875%, CF 0.8870. Source: *CME Treasury Analytics, 11 Nov 2026 12:10 PM CT* (identification only; the Nov 11 snapshot's futures price is superseded). Cash price 94.188 clean / 95.12 dirty, observed Nov 10 close (Safe Rate Markets, republishing Treasury's end-of-day prices; bid 94.094 / offer 94.125), repricing to a yield of 4.894% (CME reported 4.9023%); cross-checks: DV01 \$55.03 vs CME \$53.98, modified duration 5.84 vs CME 5.78. SOFR 3.88% effective 9 Nov 2026 (NY Fed, latest FRED observation at the pull); haircut 2% (*scenario assumption*); T = 0.055y to first delivery (1 Dec 2026). CME basis net of carry −0.3539 pts. *Reported, REJECTED: it implies cash ~93.71, ~38–48c below every Nov 10 print; kept in the output for comparison only*. Futures 106.25, official Nov 10 settlement 106'080 (CME). Both legs Nov 10 vintage. Aggregate anchors: Monin (Fed, 22 June 2026), September 2025 data (basis ~\$830bn; gross \$4.0tn; repo \$3.0tn; swap-spread ~\$305bn; ~\$60bn swap-spread unwind in April 2025). CFTC COT: leveraged funds net short 2,262,310 10y contracts as of 3 Nov 2026.

*Full results.* See `outputs/basis_trade_real_ctd_results.json` / `.csv` (generated by the script) and `outputs/basis_trade_results.json` (par illustration, corrected). Headline table is in Section 3.

*Sensitivity (run on the real CTD).* Haircut 0% / 1% / 2% / 4% (leverage ∞ / 100x / 50x / 25x); repo +25 bp \$12,769 / +50 bp \$25,538 / +100 bp \$51,075 (20-day horizon: the repo shock is small only because delivery is 20 days away; on a 3-month horizon it would be ~\$116k); basis cash-cheapening 0.10 pts \$100,000 / 0.50 pts \$500,000 / 1.00 pts \$1,000,000; yield ±25 bp VM \$1,375,844 / ±50 bp \$2,751,689 / ±100 bp \$5,503,377 (VM call scales linearly with |Δy|; as % of equity: 72% / 145% / 289%).

